=== unreachable code after return still type checks
fn f() -> int {
    return 1
    "not an int"
}
--- error
3: type mismatch

=== for over non-iterable is an error
for x in 5 { print(x) }
--- error
1: not iterable

=== struct literal not allowed in if condition without parens
struct P { x: int }
let p = P { x: 1 }
if p == P { x: 1 } { print("eq") }
--- error
3: expected

=== struct literal allowed in parens in condition
struct P { x: int }
let p = P { x: 1 }
if p == (P { x: 1 }) { print("eq") }
--- stdout
eq
